Subject: [PATCH 66/66] Paired-episode analysis: dump launcher, GT-derived
 episode features, report

scripts/analysis/dump_eval.sh MODEL(baseline|try5|kd) PROTOCOL(free|forced)
RUN ITER runs one val_unseen evaluation with the decision dump; the forced
protocol lets the DAgger expert drive so every model sees the same states.
episode_features.py derives per-episode strata from the GT path, the MP3D
region boxes and connectivity graph and the instruction (forks, room
changes, decoys, spatial words, LLM-map region hit rate).
paired_report.py pairs the dumps episode by episode against the first run:
2x2 success table, hard-subset SR/SPL, discordant-pair feature profile,
failure modes, efficiency on commonly solved episodes, per-step decision
accuracy (free and forced, per-state 2x2), first-divergence analysis.
Counts and means only, no intervals.

